<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<map xmlns="http://openorienteering.org/apps/mapper/xml/v2" version="9">
    <notes>INFO (course setter to include on map)
Title:
	Eastern part: University of Canterbury
	Western part: Dovedale Campus
Scale: 1:4,000
Contour interval: 2.5m
North lines: 150m apart


CREDITS (course setter to include on map - 6pt Arial)
Cartography: Initial by L. Earnshaw 2012. 
Extended to Dovedale Campus by P. Cleary 2015
Extended to Kirkwood Intermediate by C. Cleary, L. Earnshaw 2016
Updates: C. Forne 2012, N. Smith 2015, L. Earnshaw 2016, S. Smith 2017, L. Earnshaw 2018, J. Lynch 2020, L. Earnshaw 2021, R. Moore 2022, J. Lynch 2025
Copyright © Peninsula and Plains Orienteers
Possession of this map does not imply right of access
Non-commercial use only unless otherwise granted
Map version: 65a46ed


COORDINATORS' NOTES (map coordinator to update + commit on map being sent)
Last sent to: Malcolm Ingham &lt;mandg.ingham@xtra.co.nz&gt;


CONTROLLERS' NOTES (controller to read upon map being sent)
All courses need to be approved 2-3 weeks before event with HR at Uni (see permissions).
Hazards include traffic and parked vehicles, cyclists, pedestrians, river, slippery surfaces, blind corners.
If you have an event crossing Ilam Road you need a road crossing management stragegy - seriously! It is VERY busy and dangerous. Took 4 people full time in 2016. Think about a timed crossing.

University halls need seperate permissions to UC itself - and must be asked with care. Last event was KO Sprint Apr 2025, permissions were granted for Ilam Apartments, Tupuānuku, Arcady, Sonoda (but not Hayashi).


MAPPERS' NOTES
Dovedale campus is under active construction - will require updating. The old Dovedale Village is being rebuilt during 2025, this will be a good area to add once complete.
There is a new hall that is under constructin during 2025, beside Tupuānuku.</notes>
